o a per-item approach with helpers. Single-item and multi-item policies now share the same code path.\n\nRefactor while keeping tests green. Run autonomously, return when done.\n\nNotes:\n- The restructure is clean. The main remaining smell is the awkward filter+for loop with separate runes/moonstones/nonComponentItems lists.\n- Future tests (loyalty, first insurance, follow-up contract) will require applying policy-wide modifiers on top of policyBase.\n- The Math.ceil(premium) call anticipates the rounding test (test 24), but it's not yet required for the current 19 tests.\n- DO NOT remove the Math.ceil -- it's harmless and forward-looking.\n- DO NOT consolidate the filters into a single map -- keep separate for clarity.\n- If no improvement is possible without violating the no-over-engineering rule, say so.\n- Run pnpm test. Return summary with APP mass change.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test files: src/premium.spec.ts, src/claim.spec.ts, src/scenario.spec.ts\nImplementation: src/premium.ts (heavily restructured; now uses per-item helpers itemBasePremium, itemInsuranceValue, itemPremium, plus alikeComponentBasePremium)\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green: restructured the entire quote function into a per-item approach with helpers. Single-item and multi-item policies now share the same code path.\n\nRefactor while keeping tests green. Run autonomously, return when done.\n\nNotes:\n- The restructure is clean. The main remaining smell is the awkward filter+for loop with separate runes/moonstones/nonComponentItems lists.\n- Future tests (loyalty, first insurance, follow-up contract) will require applying policy-wide modifiers on top of policyBase.\n- The Math.ceil(premium) call anticipates the rounding test (test 24), but it's not yet required for the current 19 tests.\n- DO NOT remove the Math.ceil -- it's harmless and forward-looking.\n- DO NOT consolidate the filters into a single map -- keep separate for clarity.